---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import site from '../site.config.ts';
import { url } from '../lib/url.ts';
---
<Page title="About" description={`About ${site.name}, a free rebar takeoff tool.`}>
  <p>{site.name} gives the weight of reinforcing bar from the bar size, the length and the quantity. It is built for estimators, contractors and engineers who need a number fast, in pounds, kilograms or tons.</p>
  <h2>Where the numbers come from</h2>
  <p>The weights are the nominal values in ASTM A615 for US bar sizes #3 to #18 and in ASTM A615M for the metric sizes. Plain round diameters use the density of steel, 7,850 kg per cubic meter.</p>
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <p>It handles a full list of bars, and you can copy or print the list.</p>
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>The math runs in your browser. We do not ask you to create an account. Your lines are saved on your own device so you can come back to them.</p>
  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <p>The result is an estimate from nominal weights. Real bars vary, and laps, hooks and cut-offs change the order quantity. Check the final numbers against your drawings and your supplier before you order.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions or ideas? Write to <a href={site.contactHref}>{site.contactLabel}</a> or visit the <a href={url('contact/')}>Contact page</a>.</p>
</Page>
